# Open a DoT build (allflame_exp_016, Righteous Fire) from the build list with a double-click, change the character level (a recalc) and save with Ctrl+S (Build:SaveDB, the XML written to the user dir: in memory here), type a note in the Notes tab and save again with the Save button.
screen 1920 1080
fixture userdir=../fixtures/user
frames 2
wait-idle
expect-mode LIST
step open_from_list
# double-click allflame_exp_016 in the build list: the build keeps its file name, so Save writes it
move 700 131
click LEFTBUTTON
click LEFTBUTTON
frames 4
wait-idle
expect-mode BUILD
expect-recalc
snapshot loaded
step edit_level
move 945 14
click LEFTBUTTON
frames 2
expect-recalc
step save_ctrl_s
key-down CTRL
press s
key-up CTRL
frames 2
expect-file-write
snapshot saved
expect-differs loaded saved
step notes
key-down CTRL
press 6
key-up CTRL
frames 2
expect-tab NOTES
move 900 400
click LEFTBUTTON
frames 1
type "Profiling note: level changed, saved twice."
frames 2
# the note is in the edit box (a missed click or lost typing fails here)
expect-text "Profiling note: level changed"
step save_button
move 96 14
click LEFTBUTTON
frames 2
expect-file-write
